1. ENGINEERING PURPOSE
The Geometry & Parametric Model Engine is the computational layer between the OneDraft Project Model and the documentation system.
It is responsible for converting semantic architectural objects into deterministic geometric representations.
The engine must support:
buildings
levels
grids
spaces
walls
doors
windows
slabs
roofs
columns
beams
foundations
stairs
ramps
openings
assemblies
connections
annotations references
and future architectural, structural, mechanical, electrical and civil objects.
The geometry engine does not replace the Project Model.
It derives geometry from the Project Model.
The fundamental relationship is:
PROJECT REQUIREMENTS
        ↓
PROJECT MODEL
        ↓
PARAMETRIC OBJECTS
        ↓
CONSTRAINT SOLVER
        ↓
GEOMETRY ENGINE
        ↓
GEOMETRY VERSION
        ↓
DOCUMENTATION ENGINE
        ↓
DRAWINGS

2. CORE ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLE
OneDraft must never treat a drawing as the authoritative representation of the building.
The authoritative representation is:
SEMANTIC PROJECT MODEL
+
PARAMETERS
+
RELATIONSHIPS
+
CONSTRAINTS
+
GEOMETRY
A drawing is generated from that state.
Therefore:
MODEL → DRAWING
rather than:
DRAWING → MODEL
This permits the same project state to generate:
plans
elevations
sections
details
3D views
schedules
quantities
coordination information
rendering geometry
and future export formats.

