19. SPACES
Spaces shall be derived from boundaries.
A space is not merely a manually entered area.
Its area is calculated from its boundary geometry.
Conceptually:
BOUNDARY
   ↓
CLOSED LOOP
   ↓
PLANAR REGION
   ↓
AREA
   ↓
VOLUME

20. SPACE BOUNDARY
The engine shall detect or explicitly receive:
boundary curves
The curves must form a valid closed region.
Validation must identify:
open boundary
self-intersection
duplicate edge
zero-length edge
invalid orientation

21. SPACE AREA
For a valid planar region:
Area = geometric area of region
The calculated value shall be stored as derived data.
It must be possible to regenerate it from the geometry.

22. SPACE VOLUME
Where a valid vertical extent exists:
Volume = Area × Height
For irregular spaces the engine shall use solid intersection and volume calculation.

